note aien-supervise: AIEN's process supervisor, no systemd. One unprivileged daemon per operator
note account (cron @reboot + per-minute `ensure`) runs the services declared in
note   ~/.config/aien-supervise/services/NAME.svc   (user services: run as this account), and
note   /etc/aien-supervise/services/NAME.svc        (sandboxed services: started through
note                                                 `sudo -n aien-supervise-root run NAME`).
note It restarts with exponential backoff, runs oneshot services on a period (timers), pipes each
note service's output into state/log/NAME.log with size rotation, and takes start/stop/restart
note requests through state/ctl. Commands: run | ensure | status [NAME] | start|stop|restart NAME
note | check [NAME] | shutdown.
text tsudo "/usr/bin/sudo"
text tdn "-n"
text tenv "/usr/bin/env"
text tdi "-i"
text tnice "/usr/bin/nice"
text twatch "/usr/local/libexec/aien-supervise/aien-watch"
text thelp "/usr/local/libexec/aien-supervise/aien-supervise-root"
text trdir "/etc/aien-supervise/services"
text tlst "/.local/state/aien-supervise"
text tlcf "/.config/aien-supervise/services"
text thome "HOME"
text estate "AIEN_SUPERVISE_STATE"
text euser "AIEN_SUPERVISE_USERDIR"
text eroot "AIEN_SUPERVISE_ROOTDIR"
text ehelp "AIEN_SUPERVISE_HELPER"
text tselfx "/proc/self/exe"
text tdevnul "/dev/null"
text dctl "/ctl"
text dst "/st"
text dlog "/log"
text fpid "/daemon.pid"
text flog "/daemon.log"
text flast ".last"
text xlog ".log"
text xtmp ".tmp"
text dot "."
text vrun "run"
text vstop "stop"
text vkill "kill"
text vstart "start"
text vrestart "restart"
